{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mn5RTLcoL7m4mt4dVDhp2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\tEntry point for the coding agent that runs this repo. Humans want\n4\t[`README.md`](README.md). The daily pipeline that calls you is described in\n5\t[`pipeline/README.md`](pipeline/README.md); the prompt you were handed tells\n6\tyou which phase you are in.\n7\t\n8\t## What this repo is\n9\t\n10\t**One m0saic template a day, written by an AI agent, built in public.** Every\n11\tday a fresh agent run scouts the web for a media workflow that needs support,\n12\tplans a media solution, builds one template (variants allowed), critiques it,\n13\tand ships the one that clears the gate. `journal/YYYY-MM-DD/` is the record of\n14\teach day; `src/` is the shelf of templates; `dist/` + `template-manifest.json`\n15\tare what Mosaic Desktop and the m0saic CLI load. `TEMPLATES.md` is the\n16\tdirectory page people browse on GitHub; the build writes it from the manifest\n17\t(`tools/gen-gallery.mjs`) - never edit it by hand.\n18\t\n19\tThis is a **third-party** template repo: the namespace is `@one-a-day`, it is\n20\tnot signed, and hosts show it as `3P`. Nobody reviews a day before it ships\n21\texcept the gate. That is the point, and it is why the rules below are hard.\n22\t\n23\tThe agent that runs today may be Claude, Codex, Kimi or another CLI. Nothing\n24\there assumes which. Your model name goes into `journal/<date>/run.json` as\n25\t`model.selfDeclared`; a human may correct it later.\n26\t\n27\t## Before you write a template: the knowledge base and the examples\n28\t\n29\tThe reasoning behind every rule here lives in **`@m0saic/knowledge`** — the m0\n30\thandbook, the engine mental models, the template-authoring contract, as plain\n31\tMarkdown. After `npm install` it is at `node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/README.md`\n32\t(start there, then `docs/m0saic-thesis.md`, then the router `docs/README.md`);\n33\ton GitHub at [m0saic-packages/packages/knowledge](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-packages/tree/main/packages/knowledge).\n34\tThe pages that pay for themselves on a template day:\n35\t\n36\t- `docs/templates/philosophy-and-contract.md` — what a template is and promises\n37\t- `docs/templates/construction-strategy.md` — how to build the layout\n38\t- `docs/templates/standalone-pack-authoring.md` — the authoring loop in a repo like this\n39\t- `docs/handbook/feasibility-precision-quantization.md` — before any geometry\n40\t- `docs/runtime/cli-usage.md` — the CLI, its exit codes, `--validate-only`\n41\t\n42\tThen read code. Three public repos cover most of the product surface:\n43\t\n44\t- [m0saic-template-repo-starter](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-template-repo-starter)\n45\t  — ~80 one-concept lessons; copy a pattern in isolation.\n46\t- [m0saic-community-templates](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-community-templates)\n47\t  — the public library, one folder per publisher, signed releases.\n48\t- [m0saic-packages/packages/templates](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-packages/tree/main/packages/templates)\n49\t  — the official library that ships in the product; the house standard.\n50\t\n51\t## The files that are your memory\n52\t\n53\tA day is several fresh agent calls. Nothing survives between them except files:\n54\t\n55\t```\n56\tjournal/<date>/state.json      phase ledger: <phase>: \"done\"; decision, pick, useCase, pack, slug…\n57\tjournal/<date>/run.json        who ran; model.selfDeclared (yours); phase outcomes (the runner's)\n58\tjournal/<date>/10-scout.md     candidates, evidence, the pick\n59\tjournal/<date>/20-brief.md     the spec the critic scores against\n60\tjournal/<date>/30-build.md     what each variant tried\n61\tjournal/<date>/40-critique.md  scores, SHIP <x> | NO SHIP\n62\tjournal/<date>/40-critique.r<n>.md  an earlier NO SHIP today; revision round n answers it (state.json `revision`)\n63\tjournal/<date>/50-ship.md      what shipped, the render one-liner, weak spots\n64\tjournal/<date>/variants/<x>/   src/ + renders/ + stills/ + report.json per variant\n65\tjournal/index.json             one row per day (the runner writes it) — read it to avoid repeats\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tRead the day's files before acting. Mark a phase done in `state.json` only when\n69\tits output file is complete; the runner re-calls a phase until it sees the key.\n70\t\n71\tA critic's NO SHIP is a review, not the end of the day: the runner moves the\n72\tverdict aside as `40-critique.r<n>.md`, sets `state.json.revision = n`, and\n73\tcalls the build again to answer it — same id, same folder, the next variant\n74\tletter — and then the critic again. Your prompt says when you are in a round.\n75\t\n76\t## The loop\n77\t\n78\t```\n79\tnpm run new -- <pack>/<slug> --title \"Human Title\"   # scaffold: template + test + registry wiring (+ pack)\n80\tnpm run build          # check-freeze → tsc → copy assets → manifest → conventions gate (renders every template at defaults)\n81\tnode tools/check-registry.mjs --json    # the gate's findings as JSON, each with its fix — loop on this\n82\tnpm test               # jest (src/**/*.test.ts) + the pipeline's own tests\n83\tnpm run fingerprints:update             # after an intended layout change (commits <slug>.layout.m0 beside the template)\n84\tnode pipeline/render/render-variant.mjs @one-a-day/<pack>/<slug>/v1 journal/<date>/variants/a\n85\t                       # build + render landscape/portrait/square + stills + report.json + a copy of the source folder\n86\tnpm run previews       # mint the browse card (ship phase only; needs the CLI + paid tier);\n87\t                       # a video template also gets preview.gif, the loop TEMPLATES.md plays\n88\tnpm run verify         # build + lint + jest + loader contract + dependency policy — the gate runs this\n89\tm0saic doctor . --json # the same conventions from outside the build\n90\tm0saic make @one-a-day/<pack>/<slug>/v1 --template-repo . --tutorial -w 1280 -h 720 -o why.mp4\n91\t                       # the why-tutorial as a clip (render-variant does this for you)\n92\tnode tools/check-why.mjs --json         # the why-tutorial gate's findings (the build runs it last)\n93\t```\n94\t\n95\t**`tsc --noEmit` is a weaker signal than `npm run build`.** **The CLI renders\n96\t`dist/`, so rebuild before you render.** **Exit 0 is not a picture:** `m0saic\n97\tmake` exits **3** when it rendered an error mosaic — `render-variant` reports\n98\tit as `degraded`; treat it as a failure.\n99\t\n100\t## Adding a template — the whole checklist\n101\t\n102\t1. `npm run new -- <pack>/<slug> --title \"<Title>\"` — one template per day,\n103\t   `v1`, under an existing pack when one fits (`pipeline/config.json` lists the\n104\t   preferred vocabulary; a new pack needs a sentence of justification). The\n105\t   scaffold titles it `YYYY-MM-DD · <Title>` and tags it with the date and\n106\t   `day-NNN`: hosts sort the grid by name or by first tag, so the day is the\n107\t   ordinal and a search for a date finds the template. Keep both as written.\n108\t2. Edit `src/<pack>/<slug>/v1/<slug>.ts`. The header comment is the lesson:\n109\t   what it makes, for whom, the one rule that bites. Keep the scaffold's shape:\n110\t   typed props with deterministic defaults, `bindProp` on the rects that show a\n111\t   prop, `svgLabel` copy that fits its cell, geometry from `ctx.target`,\n112\t   fail-fast validation in `render()`, `outputHints` with a `format`, and the\n113\t   layout contract (below): tag every source, declare what the geometry\n114\t   promises, return `withLayoutIntent(...)`.\n115\t   Then the row the scaffold added to `src/<pack>/registry.ts`: its\n116\t   `description` and `tags` are what the manifest, a host's Templates page and\n117\t   `TEMPLATES.md` show - NOT the ones in the template file. Replace the\n118\t   scaffold's placeholder description with your one line and add your search\n119\t   tags after the pack, date and day (or pass `--description` to `npm run\n120\t   new`). Once the template has its own description, the build refuses a row\n121\t   that still carries the placeholder.\n122\t3. Edit the test beside it to assert what the brief claims (bindings, floors,\n123\t   determinism, a validation error).\n124\t4. Fill `WHY` — the why-tutorial spec (see the section below). The scaffold\n125\t   pre-filled day, date, agent, model, the use case and the sources from the\n126\t   journal; you write the words. The build refuses a leftover `[fill me]`.\n127\t5. `npm run build` clean, `npm test` green, fingerprints updated.\n128\t6. Render variants with `render-variant.mjs`; the critic judges the stills and\n129\t   reports — including the tutorial's pages (`stills/tutorial-<n>.png`). Ship\n130\t   phase: `npm run build && npm run previews && npm run build && npm run fingerprints:update && npm run verify`.\n131\t7. Write the journal. Do not commit — the runner does, once, after its gate.\n132\t\n133\t## The layout contract — every template says what its geometry promises\n134\t\n135\tText is the #1 defect an agent ships: svg text never wraps or shrinks by\n136\titself, and an unfitted string clips silently. So every template declares a\n137\tcontract and the build sweeps it (`tools/check-layout.mjs`, after the\n138\tplatform conventions) at the seven contract canvases — 1920x1080 · 1280x720\n139\t· 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160 · 640x360 · 480x270 — at the template's\n140\tdefaults; the template's own test sweeps it for the copy that stresses it\n141\t(`sweepLayout` from `src/_shared/layout.ts`).\n142\t\n143\tWhat to promise — the general tidiness of one template, not pixel positions:\n144\t\n145\t- **every text fits its box** — `tag(src, label)` every text source and give\n146\t  each label a `textFits`. Use `textFitsMeasured(label, text, px, width)` when\n147\t  you measured the block yourself (exact), or `textFitsAll(labels, {\n148\t  charWidthEm: TEXT_EM.prose })` for `svgLabel` copy (the bundled font's\n149\t  calibrated ruler; the contract's default 0.72 is for an unknown font and\n150\t  flags a full-width line that fits). A label is one-to-many: give cells with\n151\t  different copy different labels.\n152\t- **the chrome lives where the design says** — `within: { yFrac: [0.6, 1] }`\n153\t  for a footer band, `minWidthFrac: 0.98` for a full-width bar, `aspect: 1`\n154\t  for a mark, a bare `{ label }` when the element must simply be there.\n155\t- **only what the brief demands** — pin an exact fraction (\"the header is\n156\t  18% tall\") only when the observed use case asks for it.\n157\t\n158\tWire it as `return withLayoutIntent(doc, ctx, { templateId: ID, constraints,\n159\tdebug: props.debugLayout === true })` with a `debugLayout` boolean knob\n160\t(default false): in Make, flipping it draws the contract over the render.\n161\tDebug-only at render by ruling — a violation never blocks a real render;\n162\tthe build and the test are where it bites. A violation is a design\n163\tdecision: shrink, compact the wording, drop the row — never ellipsis at the\n164\tfloor. Fit copy at `cell * 0.94 - 2px` so quantization's pixel or two never\n165\ttips the check.\n166\t\n167\t## The harness — fixtures every template can build on\n168\t\n169\t`src/harness/` holds `internal: true` templates the shared pages and the\n170\tdaily templates use — today `@one-a-day/harness/agent-timeline/v1`, the card\n171\tthe why-tutorial ends with. Human-maintained: a day's template never lands\n172\tthere (the gate refuses it), and harness entries carry no date prefix.\n173\t\n174\t## The why-tutorial — every template explains itself\n175\t\n176\tMake has no prose surface and a link preview has no README, so each template\n177\tcarries the day's story as its `renderTutorial`: press the \"?\" pill in Make,\n178\tor `m0saic make <id> --template-repo . --tutorial -o why.mp4`. It is ONE\n179\tshared structure (`src/_shared/why.ts`, `whyTutorial(WHY, render)`), five\n180\tsteps, each its own page a viewer scrubs:\n181\t\n182\t1. **cover** — the run: day, date, which agent, which model (self-declared)\n183\t2. **the problem** — who was observed with what recurring problem, in the\n184\t   evidence's own words, and the online sources the agent actually opened\n185\t3. **the solution** — what this template attempts about it, the one design\n186\t   decision that matters, known weak spots\n187\t4. **use it** — the render one-liner and props worth trying\n188\t5. **the template itself**, rendered at its own defaults\n189\t6. **how it was made** — the harness agent-timeline card: the run's phases\n190\t   as a waterfall, tool calls, tokens AND dollars (devs read tokens,\n191\t   leadership reads dollars), wall time, and where the numbers came from\n192\t\n193\t`WHY` is a literal in the template file, frozen with it. `npm run new`\n194\twrites it pre-filled from `journal/<date>/` (`state.json` `useCase`, `who`,\n195\t`sources`; `run.json` `runner.adapter`, `model.selfDeclared`;\n196\t`trace.json` for the timeline so far). The runner writes\n197\t`journal/<date>/trace.json` from the agent CLI's own event stream after\n198\tevery phase call — tool calls, tokens, cost as the CLI reported it or an\n199\testimate from `pipeline/config.json` `pricing` (dated). In the ship phase,\n200\tcopy it into `WHY.timeline`:\n201\t\n202\t```\n203\tnode pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/<date>/trace.json\n204\t```\n205\t\n206\tThe build (`tools/check-why.mjs`) refuses a placeholder, non-ASCII copy, a\n207\tbad URL, a `day`/`date`/`agent`/`model` that disagrees with the journal, a\n208\ttimeline that disagrees with the trace, or a tutorial that does not render\n209\tas those six steps. The critic scores whether the pages tell the truth.\n210\tBudget: 1-3 paragraphs of at most 320 characters per page — it is\n211\torientation; the detail is the journal.\n212\t\n213\t## Rules that fail silently\n214\t\n215\t- **`ctx.target`, never `ctx.output`** — they agree until the template renders nested.\n216\t- **Never guess a `flattenedStableKey`** — compute it with `findStableKeys`. A wrong key renders *silently black* and exits 0.\n217\t- **`export *` only** in pack index files. Pairing it with a named re-export of the same module fills `templates[]` with `undefined`.\n218\t- **ASCII only in rendered copy** — the bundled glyph font draws `→` as tofu (the gate checks glyph coverage).\n219\t- **Blank lines are not spacing** — the svg rasterizer drops them when drawing *and* measuring. Gaps are geometry.\n220\t- **Splits above 12 must be 5-smooth** — `weightedSplit(…, { precision: 120 })`; the gate throws (`latticeSmooth`).\n221\t- **Validate any hand-written m0** with `validateM0String` from `@m0saic/dsl`.\n222\t- **Determinism** — no `Math.random()`, no clock, no ambient state. Seeds are props. The gate renders twice and diffs.\n223\t- **Every optional prop shows its default** — the gate renders with no inputs; a template that needs a file to look like anything gets skipped, not shipped.\n224\t\n225\t## Hard rules (the runner reverts the day if you break one)\n226\t\n227\t- Never `git commit` / `push` / `checkout` / `reset` / `tag`, never `npm publish`,\n228\t  never `npm run submit` (that is the maintenance ritual for work ON the repo;\n229\t  it refuses to run inside a day).\n230\t- Never edit `pipeline/`, `tools/`, `.github/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`,\n231\t  `package.json`, `dep-allowlist.json`, `frozen.manifest.json`, or another day's journal.\n232\t- **Shipped templates are frozen.** Never modify a `src/<pack>/<slug>/vN/` that exists\n233\t  at HEAD; `tools/check-freeze.mjs` fails the build and the gate reverts it. A fix is a\n234\t  new `vN+1` folder with `deprecated: { replacement }` on the old one — and that is a\n235\t  future day's work, not today's.\n236\t- **At most one new template folder per day.** Variants share the id and folder.\n237\t- **Never set `M0SAIC_ROOT`.** Renders run on the machine's real m0saic root\n238\t  (`~/m0saic`: the paid license, the pinned toolchain, the trust file). A\n239\t  fresh root renders stills with a free-tier mark and then every video render\n240\t  — the why-tutorial — hangs in ffmpeg (`FFMPEG_STALLED`). A permission error\n241\t  on `~/m0saic/cache/masks` (`EPERM ... mask-<hash>.png`) is not something\n242\t  to wait out: rerun once, and if the same error comes back it is your\n243\t  sandbox, which may write only inside the workspace, while a new template\n244\t  always needs a mask the cache does not hold yet. No further retry and no\n245\t  template change will clear it. Do not redirect the root, and do not point\n246\t  a cache into `journal/`: quote the error in `30-build.md`, leave the phase\n247\t  unset and stop. Write access to that cache is the machine owner's to\n248\t  grant, not yours. The runner strips the variable and deletes\n249\t  `journal/<date>/cache/` and `journal/<date>/m0saic-runtime/` before it\n250\t  commits.\n251\t- **Render outputs go under `journal/<date>/`, never the repo root.** Always\n252\t  pass `-o`; `m0saic make … --validate-only --report` with no `-o` writes\n253\t  `out.validate.json` beside `package.json`. The gate deletes stray\n254\t  `out.*`/`why.*`/`*.validate.json`/`*.output.json` at the root rather than\n255\t  failing the day, but it is a smell the critic will read.\n256\t- No new dependencies (`dep-allowlist.json` mirrors what a host resolves — a new import\n257\t  compiles here and fails at load). No downloaded media into the repo. No secrets.\n258\t\n259\t## Scope\n260\t\n261\tDo not restructure packs, renumber titles, or delete templates. Do not \"improve\"\n262\tyesterday's template. Do not touch the pipeline to make today easier — write what\n263\twas hard into `30-build.md`; the humans who maintain `pipeline/` read it.\n264\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e18ce96-0f7b-4c7d-a65d-4c48f623d3d3","uuid":"34f0a51f-9d38-4cfc-a712-b167f6c21595","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:08:45.767Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\AGENTS.md","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nEntry point for the coding agent that runs this repo. Humans want\n[`README.md`](README.md). The daily pipeline that calls you is described in\n[`pipeline/README.md`](pipeline/README.md); the prompt you were handed tells\nyou which phase you are in.\n\n## What this repo is\n\n**One m0saic template a day, written by an AI agent, built in public.** Every\nday a fresh agent run scouts the web for a media workflow that needs support,\nplans a media solution, builds one template (variants allowed), critiques it,\nand ships the one that clears the gate. `journal/YYYY-MM-DD/` is the record of\neach day; `src/` is the shelf of templates; `dist/` + `template-manifest.json`\nare what Mosaic Desktop and the m0saic CLI load. `TEMPLATES.md` is the\ndirectory page people browse on GitHub; the build writes it from the manifest\n(`tools/gen-gallery.mjs`) - never edit it by hand.\n\nThis is a **third-party** template repo: the namespace is `@one-a-day`, it is\nnot signed, and hosts show it as `3P`. Nobody reviews a day before it ships\nexcept the gate. That is the point, and it is why the rules below are hard.\n\nThe agent that runs today may be Claude, Codex, Kimi or another CLI. Nothing\nhere assumes which. Your model name goes into `journal/<date>/run.json` as\n`model.selfDeclared`; a human may correct it later.\n\n## Before you write a template: the knowledge base and the examples\n\nThe reasoning behind every rule here lives in **`@m0saic/knowledge`** — the m0\nhandbook, the engine mental models, the template-authoring contract, as plain\nMarkdown. After `npm install` it is at `node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/README.md`\n(start there, then `docs/m0saic-thesis.md`, then the router `docs/README.md`);\non GitHub at [m0saic-packages/packages/knowledge](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-packages/tree/main/packages/knowledge).\nThe pages that pay for themselves on a template day:\n\n- `docs/templates/philosophy-and-contract.md` — what a template is and promises\n- `docs/templates/construction-strategy.md` — how to build the layout\n- `docs/templates/standalone-pack-authoring.md` — the authoring loop in a repo like this\n- `docs/handbook/feasibility-precision-quantization.md` — before any geometry\n- `docs/runtime/cli-usage.md` — the CLI, its exit codes, `--validate-only`\n\nThen read code. Three public repos cover most of the product surface:\n\n- [m0saic-template-repo-starter](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-template-repo-starter)\n  — ~80 one-concept lessons; copy a pattern in isolation.\n- [m0saic-community-templates](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-community-templates)\n  — the public library, one folder per publisher, signed releases.\n- [m0saic-packages/packages/templates](https://github.com/m0saic-project/m0saic-packages/tree/main/packages/templates)\n  — the official library that ships in the product; the house standard.\n\n## The files that are your memory\n\nA day is several fresh agent calls. Nothing survives between them except files:\n\n```\njournal/<date>/state.json      phase ledger: <phase>: \"done\"; decision, pick, useCase, pack, slug…\njournal/<date>/run.json        who ran; model.selfDeclared (yours); phase outcomes (the runner's)\njournal/<date>/10-scout.md     candidates, evidence, the pick\njournal/<date>/20-brief.md     the spec the critic scores against\njournal/<date>/30-build.md     what each variant tried\njournal/<date>/40-critique.md  scores, SHIP <x> | NO SHIP\njournal/<date>/40-critique.r<n>.md  an earlier NO SHIP today; revision round n answers it (state.json `revision`)\njournal/<date>/50-ship.md      what shipped, the render one-liner, weak spots\njournal/<date>/variants/<x>/   src/ + renders/ + stills/ + report.json per variant\njournal/index.json             one row per day (the runner writes it) — read it to avoid repeats\n```\n\nRead the day's files before acting. Mark a phase done in `state.json` only when\nits output file is complete; the runner re-calls a phase until it sees the key.\n\nA critic's NO SHIP is a review, not the end of the day: the runner moves the\nverdict aside as `40-critique.r<n>.md`, sets `state.json.revision = n`, and\ncalls the build again to answer it — same id, same folder, the next variant\nletter — and then the critic again. Your prompt says when you are in a round.\n\n## The loop\n\n```\nnpm run new -- <pack>/<slug> --title \"Human Title\"   # scaffold: template + test + registry wiring (+ pack)\nnpm run build          # check-freeze → tsc → copy assets → manifest → conventions gate (renders every template at defaults)\nnode tools/check-registry.mjs --json    # the gate's findings as JSON, each with its fix — loop on this\nnpm test               # jest (src/**/*.test.ts) + the pipeline's own tests\nnpm run fingerprints:update             # after an intended layout change (commits <slug>.layout.m0 beside the template)\nnode pipeline/render/render-variant.mjs @one-a-day/<pack>/<slug>/v1 journal/<date>/variants/a\n                       # build + render landscape/portrait/square + stills + report.json + a copy of the source folder\nnpm run previews       # mint the browse card (ship phase only; needs the CLI + paid tier);\n                       # a video template also gets preview.gif, the loop TEMPLATES.md plays\nnpm run verify         # build + lint + jest + loader contract + dependency policy — the gate runs this\nm0saic doctor . --json # the same conventions from outside the build\nm0saic make @one-a-day/<pack>/<slug>/v1 --template-repo . --tutorial -w 1280 -h 720 -o why.mp4\n                       # the why-tutorial as a clip (render-variant does this for you)\nnode tools/check-why.mjs --json         # the why-tutorial gate's findings (the build runs it last)\n```\n\n**`tsc --noEmit` is a weaker signal than `npm run build`.** **The CLI renders\n`dist/`, so rebuild before you render.** **Exit 0 is not a picture:** `m0saic\nmake` exits **3** when it rendered an error mosaic — `render-variant` reports\nit as `degraded`; treat it as a failure.\n\n## Adding a template — the whole checklist\n\n1. `npm run new -- <pack>/<slug> --title \"<Title>\"` — one template per day,\n   `v1`, under an existing pack when one fits (`pipeline/config.json` lists the\n   preferred vocabulary; a new pack needs a sentence of justification). The\n   scaffold titles it `YYYY-MM-DD · <Title>` and tags it with the date and\n   `day-NNN`: hosts sort the grid by name or by first tag, so the day is the\n   ordinal and a search for a date finds the template. Keep both as written.\n2. Edit `src/<pack>/<slug>/v1/<slug>.ts`. The header comment is the lesson:\n   what it makes, for whom, the one rule that bites. Keep the scaffold's shape:\n   typed props with deterministic defaults, `bindProp` on the rects that show a\n   prop, `svgLabel` copy that fits its cell, geometry from `ctx.target`,\n   fail-fast validation in `render()`, `outputHints` with a `format`, and the\n   layout contract (below): tag every source, declare what the geometry\n   promises, return `withLayoutIntent(...)`.\n   Then the row the scaffold added to `src/<pack>/registry.ts`: its\n   `description` and `tags` are what the manifest, a host's Templates page and\n   `TEMPLATES.md` show - NOT the ones in the template file. Replace the\n   scaffold's placeholder description with your one line and add your search\n   tags after the pack, date and day (or pass `--description` to `npm run\n   new`). Once the template has its own description, the build refuses a row\n   that still carries the placeholder.\n3. Edit the test beside it to assert what the brief claims (bindings, floors,\n   determinism, a validation error).\n4. Fill `WHY` — the why-tutorial spec (see the section below). The scaffold\n   pre-filled day, date, agent, model, the use case and the sources from the\n   journal; you write the words. The build refuses a leftover `[fill me]`.\n5. `npm run build` clean, `npm test` green, fingerprints updated.\n6. Render variants with `render-variant.mjs`; the critic judges the stills and\n   reports — including the tutorial's pages (`stills/tutorial-<n>.png`). Ship\n   phase: `npm run build && npm run previews && npm run build && npm run fingerprints:update && npm run verify`.\n7. Write the journal. Do not commit — the runner does, once, after its gate.\n\n## The layout contract — every template says what its geometry promises\n\nText is the #1 defect an agent ships: svg text never wraps or shrinks by\nitself, and an unfitted string clips silently. So every template declares a\ncontract and the build sweeps it (`tools/check-layout.mjs`, after the\nplatform conventions) at the seven contract canvases — 1920x1080 · 1280x720\n· 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160 · 640x360 · 480x270 — at the template's\ndefaults; the template's own test sweeps it for the copy that stresses it\n(`sweepLayout` from `src/_shared/layout.ts`).\n\nWhat to promise — the general tidiness of one template, not pixel positions:\n\n- **every text fits its box** — `tag(src, label)` every text source and give\n  each label a `textFits`. Use `textFitsMeasured(label, text, px, width)` when\n  you measured the block yourself (exact), or `textFitsAll(labels, {\n  charWidthEm: TEXT_EM.prose })` for `svgLabel` copy (the bundled font's\n  calibrated ruler; the contract's default 0.72 is for an unknown font and\n  flags a full-width line that fits). A label is one-to-many: give cells with\n  different copy different labels.\n- **the chrome lives where the design says** — `within: { yFrac: [0.6, 1] }`\n  for a footer band, `minWidthFrac: 0.98` for a full-width bar, `aspect: 1`\n  for a mark, a bare `{ label }` when the element must simply be there.\n- **only what the brief demands** — pin an exact fraction (\"the header is\n  18% tall\") only when the observed use case asks for it.\n\nWire it as `return withLayoutIntent(doc, ctx, { templateId: ID, constraints,\ndebug: props.debugLayout === true })` with a `debugLayout` boolean knob\n(default false): in Make, flipping it draws the contract over the render.\nDebug-only at render by ruling — a violation never blocks a real render;\nthe build and the test are where it bites. A violation is a design\ndecision: shrink, compact the wording, drop the row — never ellipsis at the\nfloor. Fit copy at `cell * 0.94 - 2px` so quantization's pixel or two never\ntips the check.\n\n## The harness — fixtures every template can build on\n\n`src/harness/` holds `internal: true` templates the shared pages and the\ndaily templates use — today `@one-a-day/harness/agent-timeline/v1`, the card\nthe why-tutorial ends with. Human-maintained: a day's template never lands\nthere (the gate refuses it), and harness entries carry no date prefix.\n\n## The why-tutorial — every template explains itself\n\nMake has no prose surface and a link preview has no README, so each template\ncarries the day's story as its `renderTutorial`: press the \"?\" pill in Make,\nor `m0saic make <id> --template-repo . --tutorial -o why.mp4`. It is ONE\nshared structure (`src/_shared/why.ts`, `whyTutorial(WHY, render)`), five\nsteps, each its own page a viewer scrubs:\n\n1. **cover** — the run: day, date, which agent, which model (self-declared)\n2. **the problem** — who was observed with what recurring problem, in the\n   evidence's own words, and the online sources the agent actually opened\n3. **the solution** — what this template attempts about it, the one design\n   decision that matters, known weak spots\n4. **use it** — the render one-liner and props worth trying\n5. **the template itself**, rendered at its own defaults\n6. **how it was made** — the harness agent-timeline card: the run's phases\n   as a waterfall, tool calls, tokens AND dollars (devs read tokens,\n   leadership reads dollars), wall time, and where the numbers came from\n\n`WHY` is a literal in the template file, frozen with it. `npm run new`\nwrites it pre-filled from `journal/<date>/` (`state.json` `useCase`, `who`,\n`sources`; `run.json` `runner.adapter`, `model.selfDeclared`;\n`trace.json` for the timeline so far). The runner writes\n`journal/<date>/trace.json` from the agent CLI's own event stream after\nevery phase call — tool calls, tokens, cost as the CLI reported it or an\nestimate from `pipeline/config.json` `pricing` (dated). In the ship phase,\ncopy it into `WHY.timeline`:\n\n```\nnode pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/<date>/trace.json\n```\n\nThe build (`tools/check-why.mjs`) refuses a placeholder, non-ASCII copy, a\nbad URL, a `day`/`date`/`agent`/`model` that disagrees with the journal, a\ntimeline that disagrees with the trace, or a tutorial that does not render\nas those six steps. The critic scores whether the pages tell the truth.\nBudget: 1-3 paragraphs of at most 320 characters per page — it is\norientation; the detail is the journal.\n\n## Rules that fail silently\n\n- **`ctx.target`, never `ctx.output`** — they agree until the template renders nested.\n- **Never guess a `flattenedStableKey`** — compute it with `findStableKeys`. A wrong key renders *silently black* and exits 0.\n- **`export *` only** in pack index files. Pairing it with a named re-export of the same module fills `templates[]` with `undefined`.\n- **ASCII only in rendered copy** — the bundled glyph font draws `→` as tofu (the gate checks glyph coverage).\n- **Blank lines are not spacing** — the svg rasterizer drops them when drawing *and* measuring. Gaps are geometry.\n- **Splits above 12 must be 5-smooth** — `weightedSplit(…, { precision: 120 })`; the gate throws (`latticeSmooth`).\n- **Validate any hand-written m0** with `validateM0String` from `@m0saic/dsl`.\n- **Determinism** — no `Math.random()`, no clock, no ambient state. Seeds are props. The gate renders twice and diffs.\n- **Every optional prop shows its default** — the gate renders with no inputs; a template that needs a file to look like anything gets skipped, not shipped.\n\n## Hard rules (the runner reverts the day if you break one)\n\n- Never `git commit` / `push` / `checkout` / `reset` / `tag`, never `npm publish`,\n  never `npm run submit` (that is the maintenance ritual for work ON the repo;\n  it refuses to run inside a day).\n- Never edit `pipeline/`, `tools/`, `.github/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`,\n  `package.json`, `dep-allowlist.json`, `frozen.manifest.json`, or another day's journal.\n- **Shipped templates are frozen.** Never modify a `src/<pack>/<slug>/vN/` that exists\n  at HEAD; `tools/check-freeze.mjs` fails the build and the gate reverts it. A fix is a\n  new `vN+1` folder with `deprecated: { replacement }` on the old one — and that is a\n  future day's work, not today's.\n- **At most one new template folder per day.** Variants share the id and folder.\n- **Never set `M0SAIC_ROOT`.** Renders run on the machine's real m0saic root\n  (`~/m0saic`: the paid license, the pinned toolchain, the trust file). A\n  fresh root renders stills with a free-tier mark and then every video render\n  — the why-tutorial — hangs in ffmpeg (`FFMPEG_STALLED`). A permission error\n  on `~/m0saic/cache/masks` (`EPERM ... mask-<hash>.png`) is not something\n  to wait out: rerun once, and if the same error comes back it is your\n  sandbox, which may write only inside the workspace, while a new template\n  always needs a mask the cache does not hold yet. No further retry and no\n  template change will clear it. Do not redirect the root, and do not point\n  a cache into `journal/`: quote the error in `30-build.md`, leave the phase\n  unset and stop. Write access to that cache is the machine owner's to\n  grant, not yours. The runner strips the variable and deletes\n  `journal/<date>/cache/` and `journal/<date>/m0saic-runtime/` before it\n  commits.\n- **Render outputs go under `journal/<date>/`, never the repo root.** Always\n  pass `-o`; `m0saic make … --validate-only --report` with no `-o` writes\n  `out.validate.json` beside `package.json`. The gate deletes stray\n  `out.*`/`why.*`/`*.validate.json`/`*.output.json` at the root rather than\n  failing the day, but it is a smell the critic will read.\n- No new dependencies (`dep-allowlist.json` mirrors what a host resolves — a new import\n  compiles here and fails at load). No downloaded media into the repo. No secrets.\n\n## Scope\n\nDo not restructure packs, renumber titles, or delete templates. Do not \"improve\"\nyesterday's template. Do not touch the pipeline to make today easier — write what\nwas hard into `30-build.md`; the humans who maintain `pipeline/` read it.\n","numLines":264,"startLine":1,"totalLines":264}}}
